{"findings":[{"id":"723eb8cd-9e0d-4bf6-9370-0fe9ee6e14b8","title":"First Pages deploy may fail on folder permissions","description":"`main` makes the staging directory with `mkdtempSync`, which on Linux always creates it owner-only (`0700`), and `renameSync` keeps that mode when it moves the directory to `_site`. `actions/upload-pages-artifact` packs the directory's own entry with that mode, and GitHub Pages refuses artifacts whose directories are not world-readable (`0755`) with `deployment_perms_error`, so the first deploy after the merge is expected to fail.","category":"Reliability","action_level":"action_required","attribution_status":"pending","git_sha":"ebb67dd424ddef2c6959e947ee10a396a201b1e5","location":{"file_path":"scripts/build-site.ts","start_line":192,"end_line":194,"side":"right"},"evidence":{"citations":[{"source_type":"pr_branch_file","source":"scripts/build-site.ts[190-202]"},{"source_type":"pr_branch_file","source":".github/workflows/pages.yml[48-59]"}]}},{"id":"51e2696c-6e32-4cdc-948f-c58609d06360","title":"Concurrent builds can delete each other's files","description":"`main` decides it owns the output directory with `existsSync` before `mkdirSync`, then unlinks predictable filenames on a write failure without checking who created them. If another process creates or writes to that directory between those steps, the failed build can remove that process's site files or empty directory.","category":"Reliability","action_level":"remediation_recommended","attribution_status":"implemented","git_sha":"ebb67dd424ddef2c6959e947ee10a396a201b1e5","location":{"file_path":"scripts/build-site.ts","start_line":181,"end_line":182,"side":"right"},"evidence":{"citations":[{"source_type":"pr_branch_file","source":"scripts/build-site.ts[181-191]"},{"source_type":"pr_branch_file","source":"scripts/build-site.ts[193-202]"}]}},{"id":"afdf2ca4-e08f-4767-88ba-bf2c64bb7b8c","title":"Nested builds leave parent folders after a failed write","description":"`main` creates `options.out` and any missing parents with recursive `mkdirSync`, but its write-failure cleanup removes only the leaf directory. When a write fails for a nested output path whose parents did not exist, those newly created parents remain; the write-failure test uses only a single new directory, so it does not catch this case.","category":"Reliability","action_level":"remediation_recommended","attribution_status":"implemented","git_sha":"ebb67dd424ddef2c6959e947ee10a396a201b1e5","location":{"file_path":"scripts/build-site.ts","start_line":199,"end_line":201,"side":"right"},"evidence":{"citations":[{"source_type":"ticket","source":"https://github.com/UBayouski/tracenotes/issues/43"},{"source_type":"pr_branch_file","source":"scripts/build-site.ts[181-184]"},{"source_type":"pr_branch_file","source":"scripts/build-site.ts[196-201]"},{"source_type":"pr_branch_file","source":"tests/build-site.test.ts[147-161]"},{"source_type":"pr_branch_file","source":"scripts/build-site.ts[181-202]"},{"source_type":"pr_branch_file","source":"tests/build-site.test.ts[146-161]"},{"source_type":"pr_branch_file","source":"scripts/build-site.ts[193-201]"},{"source_type":"pr_branch_file","source":"tests/build-site.test.ts[146-159]"}]}}],"finding_state":{"complete":true,"introduced":["723eb8cd-9e0d-4bf6-9370-0fe9ee6e14b8"],"resolved":["51e2696c-6e32-4cdc-948f-c58609d06360","afdf2ca4-e08f-4767-88ba-bf2c64bb7b8c"],"still_open":[],"dismissed":[]},"review_agent_comment":"Before merging, please run the build on Linux—or at least check the `_site` directory’s permissions after a local Linux build. The workflow won’t run until after merge, and the Windows test runs can’t verify Linux directory permissions.","meta":{"analysis":{"attempted_mode":"incremental","baseline_checkpoint_id":"0499a2360c534adba579ff95d3cf1047","mode":"incremental","profile_changed":true,"reason":"changes_since_checkpoint"},"checkpoint":{"base_sha":"ebb67dd424ddef2c6959e947ee10a396a201b1e5","coverage_started_at":"2026-11-27T23:54:30.